1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,480
A father and son were trapped on

2
00:00:02,480 --> 00:00:05,820
Crete. Daedalus, the brilliant craftsman,

3
00:00:05,940 --> 00:00:07,800
could build almost anything,

4
00:00:08,240 --> 00:00:10,780
but he could not persuade King Minos

5
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:11,854
to let them go.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:15,000
So he fashioned wings from feathers and

7
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:16,740
wax. The sky,

8
00:00:16,900 --> 00:00:18,800
which no guard could patrol,

9
00:00:19,380 --> 00:00:21,320
became their path out of captivity.

10
00:00:22,620 --> 00:00:24,820
Daedalus warned his son to fly neither

11
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:27,160
too low, where sea spray would weigh

12
00:00:27,160 --> 00:00:28,020
down the feathers,

13
00:00:28,020 --> 00:00:29,640
nor too high,

14
00:00:30,020 --> 00:00:32,120
where the sun would soften their bonds.

15
00:00:33,300 --> 00:00:35,160
At first they soared together.

16
00:00:35,620 --> 00:00:37,080
Then Icarus climbed,

17
00:00:37,680 --> 00:00:40,380
overwhelmed by the freedom of flying above

18
00:00:40,380 --> 00:00:42,420
every wall he had ever known.

19
00:00:43,600 --> 00:00:45,000
Heat loosened the wax.

20
00:00:45,800 --> 00:00:49,180
Feathers scattered. Icarus plunged toward the sea

21
00:00:49,180 --> 00:00:51,000
as his father called for him,

22
00:00:51,360 --> 00:00:53,508
unable to undo what had happened.

23
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:58,420
Daedalus survived, but freedom carried a cost

24
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:00,120
he had never meant to pay.

25
00:01:00,620 --> 00:01:03,040
The story is not simply about ambition;

26
00:01:03,560 --> 00:01:06,220
it is about exhilaration outrunning judgment.
